6c2\",\n  \"input_format\": \"auto\",\n  \"selected_input_format\": \"21.01\",\n  \"tool_id\": \"toolshed.g2.bx.psu.edu/repos/bgruening/text_processing/tp_replace_in_line/9.5+galaxy3\",\n  \"tool_inputs\": {\n    \"infile\": {\n      \"id\": \"f9cad7b01a472135dff4fc8f8f53135f\",\n      \"src\": \"hda\"\n    },\n    \"replacements\": [\n      {\n        \"find_pattern\": \"Chronic Round1 S1\",\n        \"replace_pattern\": \"value\",\n        \"sed_options\": \"\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"validate_before_submit\": true\n}\n\n=== run_005 validation\n{\n  \"action\": \"/tool_runner/index\",\n  \"citations\": true,\n  \"creator\": [\n    {\n      \"class\": \"Organization\",\n      \"name\": \"European Galaxy Team\",\n      \"url\": \"https://galaxyproject.org/eu/\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"class\": \"Person\",\n      \"familyName\": \"Gr\\u00fcning\",\n      \"givenName\": \"Bj\\u00f6rn\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/bgruening\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"class\": \"Person\",\n      \"familyName\": \"Gordon\",\n      \"givenName\": \"Assaf\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/agordon\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"class\": \"Person\",\n      \"familyName\": \"Bernt\",\n      \"givenName\": \"Matthias\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/bernt-matthias/\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"credentials\": [],\n  \"description\": \"in entire line\",\n  \"display\": true,\n  \"edam_operations\": [],\n  \"edam_topics\": [],\n  \"enctype\": \"application/x-www-form-urlencoded\",\n  \"errors\": {},\n  \"form_style\": \"regular\",\n  \"has_parameters\": true,\n  \"help\": \"<p><strong>What it does</strong></p>\\n<p>This tool performs find &amp; replace operation on a specified file.</p>\\n<p class=\\\"infomark\\\">The <strong>pattern to find</strong> uses the <strong>extended regular</strong> expression syntax (same as running 'sed -r').</p>\\n<p class=\\\"infomark\\\"><strong>TIP:</strong> If you need more complex patterns, use the <em>sed</em> tool.</p>\\n<hr class=\\\"docutils\\\" />\\n<p><strong>Examples of Find Patterns</strong></p>\\n<ul class=\\\"simple\\\">\\n<li><strong>HELLO</strong>     The word 'HELLO' (case sensitive).</li>\\n<li><strong>AG.T</strong>  The letters A,G followed by any single character, followed by the letter T.</li>\\n<li><strong>A{4,}</strong>     Four or more consecutive A's.</li>\\n<li><strong>chr2[012]\\\\t</strong>   The words 'chr20' or 'chr21' or 'chr22' followed by a tab character.</li>\\n<li><strong>hsa-mir-([^ ]+)</strong>        The text 'hsa-mir-' followed by one-or-more non-space characters. When using parenthesis, the matched content of the parenthesis can be accessed with <strong>1</strong> in the <strong>replace</strong> pattern.</li>\\n</ul>\\n<p><strong>Examples of Replace Patterns</strong></p>\\n<ul class=\\\"simple\\\">\\n<li><strong>WORLD</strong>  The word 'WORLD' will be placed whereever the find pattern was found.</li>\\n<li><strong>FOO-&amp;-BAR</strong>  Each time the find pattern is found, it will be surrounded with 'FOO-' at the beginning and '-BAR' at the end. <strong>&amp;</strong> (ampersand) represents the matched find pattern.</li>\\n<li><strong>\\\\1</strong>   The text which matched the first parenthesis in the Find Pattern.</li>\\n</ul>\\n<hr class=\\\"docutils\\\" />\\n<p><strong>Example 1</strong></p>\\n<p><strong>Find Pattern:</strong> HELLO\\n<strong>Replace Pattern:</strong> WORLD</p>\\n<p>Every time the word HELLO is found, it will be replaced with the word WORLD.</p>\\n<hr class=\\\"docutils\\\" />\\n<p><strong>Example 2</strong></p>\\n<p><strong>Find Pattern:</strong> ^(.{4})\\n<strong>Replace Pattern:</strong> &amp;\\\\t</p>\\n<p>Find the first four characters in each line, and replace them with the same text, followed by a tab character. In practice - this will split the first line into two columns.</p>\\n<hr class=\\\"docutils\\\" />\\n<p><strong>Extended Regular Expression Syntax</strong></p>\\n<p>The select tool searches the data for lines containing or not containing a match to the given pattern. A Regular Expression is a pattern descibing a certain amount of text.</p>\\n<ul class=\\\"simple\\\">\\n<li><strong>( ) { } [ ] . * ? + ^ $</strong> are all special characters. <strong>\\\\</strong> can be used to &quot;escape&quot; a special character, allowing that special character to be searched for.</li>\\n<li><strong>^</strong> matches the beginning of a string(but not an internal line).</li>\\n<li><strong>(</strong> .. <strong>)</strong> groups a particular pattern.</li>\\n<li><strong>{</strong> n or n, or n,m <strong>}</strong> specifies an expected number of repetitions of the preceding pattern.<ul>\\n<li><strong>{n}</strong> The preceding item is matched exactly n times.</li>\\n<li><strong>{n,}</strong> The preceding item ismatched n or more times.</li>\\n<li><strong>{n,m}</strong> The preceding item is matched at least n times but not more than m times.</li>\\n</ul>\\n</li>\\n<li><strong>[</strong> ... <strong>]</strong> creates a character class. Within the brackets, single characters can be placed. A dash (-) may be used to indicate a range such as <strong>a-z</strong>.</li>\\n<li><strong>.</strong> Matches any single character except a newline.</li>\\n<li><strong>*</strong> The preceding item will be matched zero or more times.</li>\\n<li><strong>?</strong> The preceding item is optional and matched at most once.</li>\\n<li><strong>+</strong> The preceding item will be matched one or more times.</li>\\n<li><strong>^</strong> has two meaning:\\n- matches the beginning of a line or string.\\n- indicates negation in a character class. For example, [^...] matches every character except the ones inside brackets.</li>\\n<li><strong>$</strong> matches the end of a line or string.</li>\\n<li><strong>|</strong> Separates \n=== run_005 param prov\n{\n  \"checked_parameter_count\": 3,\n  \"mismatches\": [\n    {\n      \"expected\": \"Chronic Round1 S1\",\n      \"path\": \"replacements|0|find_pattern\",\n      \"resolved\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"expected\": \"value\",\n      \"path\": \"replacements|0|replace_pattern\",\n      \"resolved\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"expected\": \"\",\n      \"path\": \"replacements|0|sed_options\",\n      \"resolved\": null\n    }\n  ],\n  \"missing_paths\": [],\n  \"status\": \"mismatch\"\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
